2. THE COMPETITION, ITS NAME AND ITS FORMAT

The Predictathon competition has been run continuously since 1998. Separately
from, and in addition to, the rights in the Software, the copyright holder
asserts rights in:

  (a) the name "Predictathon" and the goodwill built up in it through
      continuous use since 1998;
  (b) the text of the rules of the game, the scoring tables, and all other
      written and visual material describing the competition, as original
      literary and artistic works;
  (c) the visual design, layout, branding, terminology and presentation of
      the competition and of this website; and
  (d) the accumulated competition data - fixtures, predictions, results,
      league tables, statistics and historical records - including any
      database right subsisting in it.

No licence is granted to operate, host, advertise or promote any prediction
competition under the name "Predictathon", or under any name or branding
confusingly similar to it, nor to reproduce the rules text, scoring tables or
presentation described above.

For the avoidance of doubt, and so that the scope of this Licence is not
overstated: the copyright holder does not claim a monopoly over the general
idea of a football score-prediction competition, or over any method of awarding
points for predictions. What is asserted above is the particular expression of
this competition - its name, its rules as written, its presentation and its
data - not the underlying concept.


